            <div xml:id="d267">

                <pb facs="0633" n="588" sameAs="frus:frus1964-68v31/pg588"/>

                <head>267. Memorandum for the Record<anchor n="1" xml:id="d267-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1964-08-21">August 21, 1964</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Minutes of the Meeting of the 303 Committee, 20 August 1964</item>
                </list>
                <list subtype="participants" type="description">
                    <label>PRESENT</label>
                    <item>Mr. Bundy, Ambassador Thompson, Mr. Vance, and Mr. McCone </item>
                </list>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>A special meeting of the 303 Committee was called for 1600 on 20 August
                        1964 to discuss two papers concerning Chile: a CIA paper dated 20 August
                        1964, “Supplementary Support for the Chilean Presidential Elections of 4
                        September 1964,”<anchor n="2" xml:id="d267-f2"/> and an undated CIA
                        memorandum, “Church Social and Political Projects in Chile.”<anchor n="3"
                            xml:id="d267-f3"/>
                    </item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>The first paper cited a cable of 19 August 1964 from the “Joint Embassy
                        Election Team” in Santiago<anchor n="4" xml:id="d267-f4"/> seeking
                        additional funds as the political race enters its last two and a half weeks.
                        The sum requested was [<hi rendition="#italic">less than 1 line of source
                            text not declassified</hi>], and in view of the extreme long-range
                        importance of the outcome of this political struggle, the Committee members
                        felt that this late hour request was justified.</item>
                    <pb facs="0634" n="589" xml:id="pg589"/>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>The second paper dealt with the political action program undertaken by
                            [<hi rendition="#italic">less than 1 line of source text not
                            declassified</hi>] in support of the CDP candidate. [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">less than 1 line of source text not
                            declassified</hi>], apparently on the basis of conversations with
                        various U.S. citizens, private and official, over the past year, assumed
                        that he had a tacit commitment for financial support. Although no formal
                        commitment to [<hi rendition="#italic">less than 1 line of source text not
                            declassified</hi>] was ever authorized, the Committee felt that [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">less than 1 line of source text not
                            declassified</hi>], regardless of his erroneous impression, had made
                        measurable contributions to the Frei campaign through his “front”
                        organizations and that some allocation of funds should be made to defray his
                        stated deficit of $395,000.</item>
                    <label>4.</label>
                    <item>Accordingly, the Committee approved the sum of [<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >less than 1 line of source text not declassified</hi>] as requested by
                        the “Joint Embassy Election Team” with the stipulation that no more than
                            [<hi rendition="#italic">less than 1 line of source text not
                            declassified</hi>] of this sum should be allocated to [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">less than 1 line of source text not
                            declassified</hi>] political action program deficit.<anchor n="5"
                            xml:id="d267-f5"/>
                    </item>
                </list>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Peter Jessup</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
